codex
Line numbers are for the pasted file.

- `instrument reading a DIFFERENT COPY`: lines `149`, `178`, `207`. Exact input: run `cd scripts; python build_3more_yf_capit_schist.py`. Consequence: the script reads/writes `scripts\YELLOW_FEVER...html` etc. or fails there, not necessarily the repo-root files it is meant to change.

- `check that CANNOT FAIL`: lines `22-31`. Exact input: `replace_realdata("abc", "x: 1")` returns `ab{x: 1bc` instead of raising. Consequence: a missing `realData: {` marker silently corrupts output.

- `SELECTOR KEYED TO A FORM THE CORPUS DOES NOT USE`: lines `25-29`. Exact input: `replace_realdata("realData: { a: '}'}; tail", "x: 1")`. Consequence: a `}` inside a JS string is treated as the end of `realData`, producing invalid mixed output.

- `probe keyed to the STRING A FIX REMOVES`: lines `151-153`, `180-182`, `209-211`. Exact input: rerun after the title has already been changed to the new topic title. Consequence: the script exits before checking or refreshing the rest of the generated page.

- `ZERO CONFLATED WITH ABSENT`: line `47`. Exact input: `tE: 482, tN: 493, cE: 0, cN: 0` for a single-arm proportion. Consequence: absent comparator is encoded as a real zero-sized comparator, inviting downstream divide-by-zero or false pairwise interpretation.

- `NEGATION DROPPED`: lines `142` and `217`. Exact input: text says `single-arm cohorts 1b/2/3 not randomized`, while protocol sets `rctOnly: true`. Consequence: non-randomized cohort evidence is mislabeled or filtered as RCT-only.

No `values compared AS TEXT where line endings differ`: Python universal newline read makes CRLF/LF alone not demonstrably defective here.

No merged-cell/tabulation defect found in this file.

No `STATUS CODE REPORTING THE WRAPPER` defect: no subprocess/pipe status is present.

COULD NOT DETERMINE: whether `allOutcomes` denominator binding is wrong for CAP-IT duration; missing dashboard consumer that maps outcome `tE/cE` to denominators.
